# Apex Logics — redirect table (Apache 2.4 / DreamHost)
# Repo-managed per AL-REDIRECTS. This file deploys via the existing rsync
# pipeline (.github/workflows/deploy.yml) and is NOT in the rsync exclude
# list, so it ships on every push. --delete is active on that rsync, so this
# repo copy is the only source of truth — do not hand-edit on the server,
# it will be destroyed on the next deploy.
#
# Rules: Redirect 301 only (permanent — transfers search authority).
# One rule per line, dated, attributed to the WU that caused it.
# No RewriteEngine and no caching rules here — see AL-REDIRECTS-SPEC.md §2 for
# scope boundaries. Log of what's live: REDIRECTS.md. Exception: the security
# headers block at the end of this file (AL-AUDIT2-HEADERS, 2026-11-25), which
# matches AINumbers' .htaccess.
#
# 2026-07-27 (AL-REDIRECTS survey): no rule entries yet at that time. Audited
# candidates — AL-58/AL-60 never shipped (no live URL ever existed); AL-06+16
# and AL-08+14 were combined before their individual tool pages ever went
# live (no old URLs to redirect). See REDIRECTS.md for the full audit trail.
# Renaming or retiring a tool going forward REQUIRES a Redirect 301 entry
# below — see repo/CLAUDE.md.

# 2026-07-27 (AL-AP2PROSE Part B): deprecated-term slug rename.
Redirect 301 /tools/ap2-advisor-prompt-composer/ /tools/advisor-prompt-composer/

# 2026-11-25 (AL-AUDIT2-HEADERS): security headers, matching AINumbers.
# Wrapped in IfModule so a host without mod_headers serves the site unchanged
# instead of a 500. HSTS has no includeSubDomains/preload on purpose (it would
# bind mcp.apexlogics.org and any other subdomain). frame-ancestors 'self' and
# SAMEORIGIN: only apexlogics.org pages may frame apexlogics.org pages. No
# page-content CSP yet (inline onclick handlers would break under one).
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
  Header always set Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
  Header always set X-Content-Type-Options "nosniff"
  Header always set Referrer-Policy "strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
  Header always set Content-Security-Policy "frame-ancestors 'self'"
  Header always set X-Frame-Options "SAMEORIGIN"
  Header always set Permissions-Policy "camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()"
</IfModule>
